        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement Panama China Diplomacy China warns against ‘third party’ influence as Panama Canal port dispute simmers Wang Yi also says Beijing ready to deepen cooperation with Panama City amid US pressure over operation of ports 2 -MIN READ 2 -MIN Listen Victoria Bela Published: 7:40pm, 27 May 2026 Updated: 7:56pm, 27 May 2026 Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi on Tuesday said Beijing was ready to deepen cooperation with Panama City and that third countries should not influence their bilateral ties. “China has always maintained that China-Panama relations are not directed against any third party and should not be interfered with by any third party,” Wang said, according to a foreign ministry read-out on Wednesday. Wang made the remarks while meeting with Panamanian Foreign Minister Javier Martinez-Acha on the sidelines of a high-level United Nations Security Council meeting in New York. Advertisement The meeting took place as the two countries continue to navigate their most significant rift since establishing ties, driven by a dispute over the operation of ports in the Panama Canal. The matter has drawn pressure from Washington. Beijing’s top diplomat also said China was “willing to work with Panama to uphold the original aspirations of establishing diplomatic relations, deepen pragmatic cooperation, eliminate external interference, and promote the healthy and stable development of bilateral relations”. 10:37 Why the US is worried about China’s growing influence in South America Martinez-Acha told Wang that Panama was willing to work with China to resolve differences through dialogue and build solid trust, according to the read-out. Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
